Package: mosaik
Type: Package
Title: Draw, Modify and Measure Landscape Patterns
Description: Draw, modify and measure spatial patterns in gridded landscape
    mosaics. Following the Unix principle, each operator does one thing and
    all of them take and return a mosaik, so that an analysis, including a
    new metric, is a combination of operators rather than a new function,
    and can be checked part by part and rerun from its recorded
    provenance. Draw operators produce abstract test fields of known
    structure, modify operators transform categorical and continuous layers,
    measure operators quantify the primitives (adjacency, area, perimeter,
    distance, dissimilarity) at patch, class, and landscape scale, and
    composite metrics are derived from equations over them. Cell values are
    group identifiers throughout, and provenance is recorded in the
    vocabulary of the W3C PROV ontology as operations are applied.
Version: 1.0.0
